1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:16,427
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

3
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:22,308
2016

4
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:24,686
EPISODE 2

5
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:36,406
I reserved this room.

6
00:02:38,741 --> 00:02:39,576
Oh, really?

7
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:44,497
Sorry.

8
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:56,217
You're here early.

9
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,223
Weren't you coming
to the practice room today?

10
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:10,565
Hey, you really don't remember me?

11
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:16,654
We met at a competition
when we were kids and had fun.

12
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:18,031
I don't remember.

13
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:19,991
Seriously?

14
00:03:20,491 --> 00:03:22,577
Come on, think carefully.

15
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:25,371
You lent me your handkerchief
when I asked.

16
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:28,625
And when we played four hands,
we clicked so well that--

17
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:30,960
I said I don't remember, so cut it out.

18
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,129
I told you yesterday.

19
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,423
I can't stand people
acting friendly with me.

20
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:44,224
What's his problem?
Why did he get so worked up?

21
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:46,976
2026 4TH QUARTER PRACTICAL LESSON FEES

22
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:51,814
What?

23
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:53,691
These are the practical lesson fees?

24
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:56,277
How many zeros is that?
Four, five, six…

25
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:57,737
Two million and…

26
00:03:57,820 --> 00:03:59,072
It's over two million won?

27
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:02,408
Don't overthink it.

28
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:05,620
It's a scholarship for being gifted.

29
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:07,705
Why do you feel so pressured?

30
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:10,667
I had no idea it'd be so expensive.

31
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:12,085
Hey.

32
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,754
Our school foundation

33
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,382
has a ton of money.

34
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,052
Besides, this isn't free.

35
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:23,554
It's a win-win

36
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:26,766
for both you and the school
when you become famous later.

37
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:31,729
I just want to graduate high school.

38
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,775
Why don't you have any ambition?

39
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,820
You have a talent others would die for.

40
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:45,660
Pay up first.

41
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:48,871
You're relentless.

42
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:02,302
I'm sorry.

43
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:06,014
Professor Seo says he can't step out
because he's busy teaching.

44
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:07,348
I'm really sorry.

45
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,816
<i>We even had a meeting a few days ago</i>

46
00:05:16,899 --> 00:05:18,860
<i>because both orchestras</i>
<i>wanted him so badly.</i>

47
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,946
<i>But when I called today,</i>
<i>they'd both changed their minds.</i>

48
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:24,490
When I kept pressing them,

49
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,284
they finally admitted

50
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:29,662
Professor Seo demanded
that they choose either him or Pi-o.

51
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,332
<i>Can you believe that man?</i>

52
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:34,459
<i>That's his own student.</i>

53
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:38,046
<i>Is he trying to ruin Pi-o's career</i>
<i>because he acted out a bit?</i>

54
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,986
How are you going to fix this?

55
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:04,864
Do you have any idea what you've done?

56
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:08,826
Why did you challenge Professor Seo
without thinking it through?

57
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,627
So what do you want me to do?

58
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,049
Just go study abroad.

59
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:25,676
You think this is a joke?

60
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,138
Professor Seo told everyone
not to give you lessons,

61
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,349
so there's no way
to get you a new teacher.

62
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:32,934
Even the concerto fell through.

63
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:35,228
We worked so hard to get here.

64
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:37,313
How could you ruin everything overnight?

65
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:40,817
You're better off studying abroad.

66
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:44,946
You can't make it here,
and you would've studied abroad anyway.

67
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,573
Just think of it as going a bit early.

68
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:48,783
I already told you.

69
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:52,245
I'm not going anywhere
until I get Grandfather's approval.

70
00:06:54,163 --> 00:06:56,791
You think I'd run off
to study abroad like a coward?

71
00:06:58,751 --> 00:06:59,752
Pi-o.

72
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:01,587
Kang Pi-o!

73
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:11,681
So?

74
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:13,015
Are you happy now?

75
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:16,394
What did you say
to get under his skin like that?

76
00:07:16,477 --> 00:07:19,230
Is your goal to make him
quit the piano by any means?

77
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:21,816
Father!

78
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:48,384
Welcome.

79
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:00,897
Where are you going at this hour?

80
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:03,816
- Heading to school?
- What do you care?

81
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,943
Jeez, you're prickly.

82
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:07,195
What did I ever do to you?

83
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:09,864
You want the receipt?

84
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,201
Huh?

85
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:31,385
Welcome.

86
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:35,139
Huh? What's this?

87
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,516
Why is he here?

88
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:37,934
Wait, is he one of those?

89
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:39,560
An equity-based admit?

90
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,521
Oh, right.

91
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:47,443
That's more annoying
than buying your way in with donations.

92
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:53,199
Jeez.

93
00:08:57,411 --> 00:08:58,621
<i>Itadakimasu.</i>

94
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:02,166
We don't sell alcohol to minors.

95
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,252
Whatever, you punk.

96
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:06,629
Save it and ring this up.

97
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:08,756
Don't you understand Korean?

98
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,883
We don't sell alcohol to minors.

99
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:15,555
Look, we get that you work hard,
but just ring us up already.

100
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:17,181
You want a hard time at school?

101
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:20,268
No, but if you're going to act like this,
respectfully get the hell out.

102
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:22,353
Why you…

103
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:24,939
Be a good charity case
and know your place.

104
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:26,482
Who do you think you are?

105
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,441
Hey.

106
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:29,735
Stop trying to look tough

107
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:31,195
and just hit me already.

108
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,905
I'll gladly take
the easy settlement money.

109
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:35,032
Hit me.

110
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:38,953
Okay.

111
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,122
Okay.

112
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:43,583
This is enough, right?

113
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:52,633
Man, the bag ripped open.

114
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,678
Oh no, my hand slipped.

115
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:58,180
- Sweet.
- Damn it.

116
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:01,434
You might as well clean the whole place.

117
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,108
Those bastards…

118
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:11,152
Hey, who were those guys on camera?

119
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:13,696
Look at this mess!

120
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:18,451
What were you doing
while the store was getting trashed?

121
00:10:19,201 --> 00:10:21,203
- I'm sorry.
- Damn it.

122
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:24,332
Who the hell were those bastards?

123
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:27,335
Right, where's your parental consent form?

124
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:29,795
The thing is…

125
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:34,383
my parents aren't around.

126
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,844
Get out of here, you punk!

127
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,388
Sir, I'm really sorry.

128
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:42,808
Damn it.

129
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:43,726
Sir…

130
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,153
Damn it.

131
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,615
- Let's get you in.
- What took you so long?

132
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:00,117
It's freezing out here.

133
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:02,703
Let's go.

134
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:17,093
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
NAGWON MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

135
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:28,789
CHOI JEONG-YO

136
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,297
<i>I'm sure the composer</i>

137
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:39,216
<i>wrote this piece to comfort someone.</i>

138
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:42,845
<i>So instead of focusing on the notes,</i>

139
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:45,639
<i>think about the emotions</i>
<i>the composer wanted to convey</i>

140
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:47,641
<i>as you play, okay?</i>

141
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,651
LIKE SOOTHING A WOUNDED HEART

142
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:26,305
CHOI JEONG-YO

143
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,152
That arrogant jerk.

144
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,738
Hey, Jerk Number Two is here.

145
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,634
Hey, what's this now?

146
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:05,928
He really must be a charity case.

147
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,847
You're using copies
because you can't afford sheet music?

148
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:11,058
- Give it back.
- I don't think so.

149
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,228
Come and get it if you can.

150
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:15,646
Give it back!

151
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:17,481
What's the matter with them?

152
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:20,651
This is why
you shouldn't have pissed me off!

153
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:22,403
- Don't do it!
- Shit.

154
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,547
Do you realize what that sheet music was?

155
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:44,842
You crazy bastard!

156
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,345
- Stop them.
- What do we do?

157
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:51,390
Shit.

158
00:14:58,439 --> 00:14:59,690
- You bastard!
- Someone stop him!

159
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,363
Come on, someone stop him!

160
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:20,878
Will he face disciplinary action?

161
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:22,046
Pi-o.

162
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:23,172
Pi-o!

163
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:27,051
Is it true Choi Jeong-yo
is facing a disciplinary hearing?

164
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,010
Yeah.

165
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:30,262
Oh no.

166
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,723
What if he ends up getting disciplined?

167
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:35,225
Anyone who uses violence
deserves punishment.

168
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:37,144
Hey, how could you say that?

169
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:39,647
Those two started it, didn't they?

170
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:42,483
It's not the first time
those jerks have played dirty.

171
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:46,904
Damn it.

172
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:48,238
Hey, Pi-o!

173
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:49,365
Where are you going?

174
00:15:58,707 --> 00:16:01,251
LIKE SOOTHING A WOUNDED HEART

175
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:07,132
Do you realize what that sheet music was?

176
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:19,812
Who the hell are you?

177
00:16:20,771 --> 00:16:22,106
Are you a thug or something?

178
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:26,110
Just how low do you have to be
to mess up our boys' faces like that?

179
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:27,736
Now what?

180
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:30,072
What are you going to do about it?

181
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:31,323
I'm very sorry.

182
00:16:32,199 --> 00:16:34,910
The school will pay
for both students' hospital bills.

183
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:37,162
He's the one who caused trouble.

184
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:39,873
So why is the school
paying the hospital bills?

185
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,418
- Well…
- Besides,

186
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,712
why aren't his parents here?

187
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:45,671
As his teacher,

188
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:48,340
I'm here in their place,
so you can speak with me.

189
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:49,258
I'll ask again.

190
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,302
Why is his teacher here
instead of his parents?

191
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:55,264
I don't have any parents,
so just talk to me.

192
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:59,018
No wonder.

193
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:01,687
I could tell
you didn't have a proper upbringing.

194
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,815
What about Jang Seok-hwan?

195
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:08,694
You think it looks like
he had a good upbringing?

196
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:10,279
- Jeong-yo!
- What did you say?

197
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:12,614
You uneducated bastard.

198
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,283
- You little punk.
- Ma'am.

199
00:17:14,366 --> 00:17:16,201
- You dare badmouth Seok-hwan?
- Please calm down.

200
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:22,875
I'll mess up your face too, you punk.

201
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:24,251
Please take a seat, ma'am.

202
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:44,897
I just have one question.

203
00:17:45,522 --> 00:17:47,941
How did a student with no parents

204
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,651
get transferred to this school?

205
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:51,945
He was selected as a gifted scholar.

206
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:53,447
"Gifted"?

207
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:54,573
Yes.

208
00:17:56,617 --> 00:18:01,622
Just how talented is he
that he can be so ill-mannered

209
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:04,249
and still earn a scholarship?

210
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:07,252
Was he even chosen fairly?

211
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,671
Whatever, I don't care.

212
00:18:10,964 --> 00:18:13,801
I refuse to forgive him,

213
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,344
so have him expelled.

214
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:18,639
I understand.

215
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:20,933
I'll have him expelled.

216
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:22,184
Ma'am!

217
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,603
Given that the two students
were badly hurt,

218
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:27,231
I'm afraid
Choi Jeong-yo will be held accountable.

219
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,858
We'll take the proper action,
so don't worry.

220
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:41,870
Seon-ju.

221
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:45,249
They were the ones who picked a fight,
so why is Jeong-yo getting expelled?

222
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:48,877
And why bother transferring him here
just to expel him over something so minor?

223
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:51,505
If he's a lost cause,
it's better to cut him loose.

224
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,924
You've seen brilliant pianists quit

225
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:56,760
because their personal lives were a mess.

226
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:00,597
This is a school, and I'm the director.

227
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:09,189
This is a school matter now,
so back off from Choi Jeong-yo.

228
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,191
Seon-ju!

229
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:16,530
<i>I'll just leave, Mr. Do.</i>

230
00:19:16,613 --> 00:19:19,366
What are you talking about, Jeong-yo?

231
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:23,495
I'll make sure
you don't get expelled, so just…

232
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:24,538
No, it's okay.

233
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:26,540
I don't think…

234
00:19:28,792 --> 00:19:30,627
I belong here anyway.

235
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:32,880
This is for the best.

236
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:36,383
Thank you for everything you've done.

237
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,558
Jeong-yo.

238
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,128
LIKE SOOTHING A WOUNDED HEART

239
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:45,535
Where are you going?

240
00:20:47,704 --> 00:20:48,956
It was nice meeting you.

241
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:50,874
Have a good life.

242
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:19,444
Jeong-yo!

243
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:22,239
Choi Jeong-yo!

244
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:41,925
Where did you get this footage?

245
00:21:42,009 --> 00:21:44,928
Is that so important right now?

246
00:21:48,056 --> 00:21:50,851
I'm not defending Choi Jeong-yo's actions.

247
00:21:52,644 --> 00:21:56,231
But taking advantage of a part-time worker
who can't defend himself

248
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:59,067
will spark public outrage.

249
00:22:00,527 --> 00:22:01,737
If you refuse to settle,

250
00:22:02,362 --> 00:22:04,823
we'll have to make this footage public.

251
00:22:05,824 --> 00:22:07,993
And you'll need to think carefully about

252
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:10,662
who will suffer from that.

253
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:20,756
Let's each compromise a bit, shall we?

254
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:34,394
Mr. Do, isn't it better if I just leave?

255
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:41,568
If you hate feeling like you owe us,

256
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:44,279
then become a great musician.

257
00:22:47,908 --> 00:22:50,660
If you leave now,
it puts us in a tight spot too.

258
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:05,133
ORIGINAL DECISION: EXPULSION
REVIEW RESULTS: EXPULSION OVERTURNED

259
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:06,426
REASON FOR REVIEW: NEW FINDINGS

260
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:16,520
That's impossible.

261
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:19,689
Why are you saying it's impossible
without even trying?

262
00:23:20,607 --> 00:23:22,067
He's incredibly talented,

263
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:27,030
but he lacks the basics
from playing however he wanted.

264
00:23:27,781 --> 00:23:29,366
He hasn't adjusted to school yet,

265
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:31,618
so I don't think we should push him.

266
00:23:31,701 --> 00:23:33,453
Hyun-soo, my pride is at stake.

267
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:37,416
Also,

268
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:40,377
if we don't prove his talent,

269
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:43,964
those people will jump at any chance
to get Jeong-yo kicked out again.

270
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:46,508
You must bring me

271
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:49,386
tangible results within a month.

272
00:23:50,637 --> 00:23:53,181
It's the only way to protect
both Jeong-yo and us.

273
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:09,906
Hi, Hyun-soo.

274
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:20,167
These days,

275
00:24:21,084 --> 00:24:23,211
kids are so open when it comes to dating.

276
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,841
We could never be that open
back in our day, right?

277
00:24:32,512 --> 00:24:34,097
It reminds me of high school.

278
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:38,059
I couldn't make my feelings obvious

279
00:24:38,935 --> 00:24:40,854
and just worried about the competition.

280
00:24:48,278 --> 00:24:50,197
Why did you come see me today?

281
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:52,407
It can't be to reminisce
about the good old days.

282
00:24:53,658 --> 00:24:54,618
Hyun-soo.

283
00:24:55,744 --> 00:24:57,370
Take Pi-o under your wing.

284
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:01,291
I know you don't want to.

285
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:04,002
It's awkward for me to ask this too.

286
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:07,881
But Pi-o refuses anyone but you,
so what choice do I have?

287
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:10,550
Don't read too much into it.

288
00:25:11,134 --> 00:25:12,636
For old times' sake,

289
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:15,514
can't you just take him on?

290
00:25:26,107 --> 00:25:27,192
- Feel the butterflies?
- Are you serious?

291
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:02,143
- No way!
- But he's cute.

292
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:03,562
- What?
- Really?

293
00:26:06,815 --> 00:26:07,816
Seriously.

294
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:10,527
Why is it so loud here?

295
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:25,584
<i>Do you still want to take lessons from me?</i>

296
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:47,439
Four hands?

297
00:26:48,023 --> 00:26:49,190
Yes.

298
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:51,526
I'll decide whether to teach you
based on that.

299
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,820
I need to be sure of you too.

300
00:26:53,903 --> 00:26:56,531
But why does it have to be four hands?

301
00:26:56,615 --> 00:27:00,243
I barely have enough time
to learn my solo repertoire.

302
00:27:00,327 --> 00:27:01,703
Wrong.

303
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:04,289
That mindset alone
shows how impatient you are.

304
00:27:05,915 --> 00:27:07,417
You think you lack skills?

305
00:27:08,251 --> 00:27:09,085
That's not true.

306
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:13,214
What you need most right now

307
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,841
is emotional connection.

308
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:18,678
And playing four hands
is the best way to feel that.

309
00:27:19,763 --> 00:27:21,890
Can I at least choose my partner?

310
00:27:21,973 --> 00:27:24,184
No, I already have someone in mind.

311
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:25,644
I'm sure you know Choi Jeong-yo.

312
00:27:25,727 --> 00:27:26,895
The new transfer student.

313
00:27:28,021 --> 00:27:29,773
The way I see it, you…

314
00:27:29,856 --> 00:27:31,566
Why him, of all people?

315
00:27:32,150 --> 00:27:34,861
He's never even had any proper lessons.

316
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:43,453
Have you listened to him play?

317
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:47,499
And you still don't know why I chose him?

318
00:27:50,293 --> 00:27:52,003
Or are you like the other kids

319
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:54,506
and don't want to hang out
with a poor classmate?

320
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:56,383
- It's not that, sir.
- Then what is it?

321
00:28:00,595 --> 00:28:03,431
Fine, let's stop here.
Forget about the lessons.

322
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:05,767
I don't want to teach someone
who's being stubborn

323
00:28:06,476 --> 00:28:07,644
from day one.

324
00:28:09,312 --> 00:28:11,147
I'll do it. Four hands.

325
00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:16,528
I'll play four hands…

326
00:28:19,614 --> 00:28:20,699
with Choi Jeong-yo.

327
00:28:34,462 --> 00:28:35,380
Thank you.

328
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:40,927
I asked to see you

329
00:28:41,010 --> 00:28:43,304
about playing
at next month's progress recital.

330
00:28:43,388 --> 00:28:44,514
Progress recital?

331
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:45,890
What's that?

332
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:48,977
It's a monthly performance
held at the school's art center.

333
00:28:51,813 --> 00:28:53,857
To put this incident behind us,

334
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:55,942
you need to show what you're capable of.

335
00:28:56,025 --> 00:28:57,861
But it'll be hard to do on your own,

336
00:28:57,944 --> 00:28:59,863
so how about playing four hands?

337
00:28:59,946 --> 00:29:01,489
Hold on, Mr. Do.

338
00:29:06,619 --> 00:29:08,288
Are you telling me…

339
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:12,333
that I need to perform?

340
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:14,210
Why? What's the problem?

341
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:17,797
Everyone at the school participates
in the progress recitals.

342
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:19,799
But…

343
00:29:22,927 --> 00:29:25,221
I'm not too confident about performing.

344
00:29:25,805 --> 00:29:27,849
No musician feels confident performing.

345
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:29,559
Everyone gets nervous.

346
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:32,771
Still…

347
00:29:33,563 --> 00:29:36,274
For now, don't argue with me

348
00:29:37,734 --> 00:29:38,777
and give it a try.

349
00:29:40,862 --> 00:29:41,863
But sir…

350
00:29:44,032 --> 00:29:45,909
Tomorrow at 6 p.m.
in the small auditorium.

351
00:29:46,701 --> 00:29:48,870
I'll text you my pick for the piece.

352
00:29:49,829 --> 00:29:51,164
Send me yours if you have any.

353
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:53,249
Wait a minute.

354
00:29:54,584 --> 00:29:57,879
We're supposed to be partners.
Shouldn't we talk things through?

355
00:29:58,463 --> 00:29:59,964
Why are you being so combative?

356
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:04,636
Does it look like I want to do this?

357
00:30:45,718 --> 00:30:47,011
Do you have any idea what time it is?

358
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:50,682
What?

359
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:55,395
Am I that late?

360
00:30:55,478 --> 00:30:57,021
Sorry, I had to eat before coming.

361
00:30:57,105 --> 00:31:00,108
You should've let me know.
Why didn't you text me?

362
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:04,279
My phone is old,
so the battery keeps dying.

363
00:31:04,362 --> 00:31:05,947
It drives me crazy too.

364
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:08,449
Let's get started.

365
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:15,915
Hey, why are you always so impatient?

366
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:19,294
I just ate. Give me some time to digest.

367
00:31:19,377 --> 00:31:21,462
Stop talking nonsense and sit down.

368
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:37,437
Hold on.

369
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:40,273
I feel so sick all of a sudden.

370
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,525
Did that food give me indigestion?

371
00:31:43,192 --> 00:31:44,694
What are you playing at?

372
00:31:46,988 --> 00:31:49,449
Hey, I don't think I can do this today.

373
00:31:49,532 --> 00:31:50,992
Let's practice tomorrow. I'm sorry.

374
00:31:51,075 --> 00:31:52,744
Hey. Hey!

375
00:31:55,038 --> 00:31:56,331
Damn it.

376
00:32:04,964 --> 00:32:05,840
Oh jeez.

377
00:32:12,889 --> 00:32:16,476
In classical poetry,
Goryeo songs have a three-beat rhythm.

378
00:32:17,060 --> 00:32:19,187
That's why they feature repeated refrains

379
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:21,856
and expressions drawn from
everyday, colloquial language.

380
00:32:22,815 --> 00:32:25,902
If a poem with a three-beat rhythm
appears on the exam,

381
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:27,362
you can assume it's a Goryeo song.

382
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:34,118
Hey.

383
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:36,037
You lied about being sick, didn't you?

384
00:32:36,704 --> 00:32:37,538
I know you did.

385
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:40,500
I really was sick!

386
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:58,309
<i>I'm sick, so I can't make it again.</i>

387
00:32:58,393 --> 00:32:59,602
<i>Let's meet at 7 a.m. tomorrow.</i>

388
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:01,771
Are you kidding me?

389
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:14,242
Are you just getting in?

390
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:16,703
Have you eaten?

391
00:33:17,537 --> 00:33:18,371
Yes.

392
00:33:23,918 --> 00:33:25,712
How are things coming along?

393
00:33:25,795 --> 00:33:27,171
Hyun-soo told me

394
00:33:27,255 --> 00:33:29,173
that you're playing
four hands with Jeong-yo.

395
00:33:32,635 --> 00:33:36,139
I told you Hyun-soo agreed
to teach Pi-o, right?

396
00:33:36,222 --> 00:33:39,767
He's in good hands with Hyun-soo,
so that's a relief.

397
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,653
Go upstairs and rest. You must be tired.

398
00:33:51,779 --> 00:33:52,697
Okay.

399
00:34:02,999 --> 00:34:04,667
<i>I'll give you one more chance.</i>

400
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,879
<i>If you're late again, I'll kill you.</i>

401
00:34:22,518 --> 00:34:23,478
6:30 A.M.

402
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:41,954
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo!

403
00:34:43,372 --> 00:34:44,582
What the heck?

404
00:34:44,665 --> 00:34:45,666
Hyun-chul!

405
00:34:46,876 --> 00:34:48,711
How did you know I was here?

406
00:34:48,795 --> 00:34:51,422
Min-su told me he saw you
wearing this school's uniform.

407
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:53,424
Why haven't you answered my calls?

408
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:54,842
Oh, sorry.

409
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:58,346
And how did you transfer to this school?

410
00:34:58,429 --> 00:35:00,389
It just kind of happened.

411
00:35:01,224 --> 00:35:02,683
So what's going on?

412
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:06,145
Let's go and talk somewhere else.

413
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:08,397
What? But I have to go…

414
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:10,691
Jeez.

415
00:35:11,692 --> 00:35:12,527
Damn it.

416
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:45,560
I stopped Min-su from running his mouth,

417
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:47,103
but Kim is raising hell right now,

418
00:35:47,186 --> 00:35:49,730
demanding the kids tell him where you are.

419
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:52,024
Damn it.

420
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:55,236
I came up with a story
saying you skipped town,

421
00:35:56,112 --> 00:35:59,365
but Kim is a persistent bastard,
and I'm worried about what he'll do.

422
00:35:59,907 --> 00:36:02,618
So keep a low profile and stay hidden.

423
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:04,370
- Got it?
- Okay.

424
00:36:07,206 --> 00:36:08,457
So he doesn't know

425
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:11,252
where my dad went?

426
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:13,754
That's what you're worried about?

427
00:36:14,755 --> 00:36:16,591
What kind of parent
ditches their kid and bolts?

428
00:36:43,951 --> 00:36:44,827
Pi-o.

429
00:36:48,456 --> 00:36:49,373
I'm sorry.

430
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:51,918
Something urgent came up.

431
00:36:58,549 --> 00:37:00,426
Want to practice during lunch break?

432
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:03,137
How do you reserve a practice room?

433
00:37:03,930 --> 00:37:06,265
I'll reserve one this time.

434
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:09,101
No, there's no need.

435
00:37:09,977 --> 00:37:10,937
Let's just drop it.

436
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:14,106
Come on, don't be like that.

437
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:16,567
Something came up, and I had no choice.

438
00:37:26,202 --> 00:37:28,746
I said I had no choice.

439
00:37:34,210 --> 00:37:35,753
You think playing the piano is a joke?

440
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:39,298
I guess it's nothing more
than fun and games to you.

441
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:41,092
But you know what?

442
00:37:42,385 --> 00:37:45,137
I hate bastards like you
who play music with that attitude.

443
00:37:48,808 --> 00:37:51,102
If you're going to act like that,
just quit school.

444
00:38:01,153 --> 00:38:03,572
That prickly little punk.

445
00:38:04,323 --> 00:38:07,535
Choi Jeong-yo? Screw him.

446
00:38:08,703 --> 00:38:09,829
Smash it more.

447
00:38:15,543 --> 00:38:18,337
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

448
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:19,880
- It'll be fine.
- Yeah, but…

449
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,716
- He won't know.
- He won't?

450
00:38:21,799 --> 00:38:22,758
I just…

451
00:38:24,176 --> 00:38:25,136
What?

452
00:38:25,219 --> 00:38:27,388
Man, he's annoying.

453
00:38:41,610 --> 00:38:42,695
Hey.

454
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:45,489
Damn it.

455
00:38:48,034 --> 00:38:48,868
Move.

456
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:56,375
Wait.

457
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:57,752
What are you doing?

458
00:39:04,675 --> 00:39:05,634
What is that?

459
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:07,762
- Who did that?
- Damn it.

460
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:09,930
Who would do that?

461
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:17,063
Someone go get the teachers.

462
00:39:20,149 --> 00:39:22,735
Hey, it was his idea!

463
00:39:23,402 --> 00:39:24,570
You traitor!

464
00:39:24,653 --> 00:39:26,322
Hey, hold on!

465
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:28,699
What are you doing?

466
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:29,617
Shit!

467
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:31,035
Wait!

468
00:39:31,118 --> 00:39:32,745
Wait! Stop!

469
00:39:32,828 --> 00:39:34,372
Stop!

470
00:39:34,455 --> 00:39:35,373
Hey.

471
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:39,001
- Stop it.
- Let go!

472
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:41,420
That bastard tried to ruin my hands!

473
00:39:42,546 --> 00:39:43,756
Are you insane?

474
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:45,758
You'll only make things worse.

475
00:39:48,719 --> 00:39:49,553
Let me see.

476
00:39:52,139 --> 00:39:53,641
Damn it.

477
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:54,725
Nurse's office. Now.

478
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:56,394
What do you care?

479
00:39:57,812 --> 00:39:59,772
Stop being stubborn.

480
00:40:00,356 --> 00:40:02,024
What if the glass
digs deeper into your skin?

481
00:40:16,038 --> 00:40:16,872
I'll do it.

482
00:40:18,082 --> 00:40:19,125
Sure.

483
00:40:24,338 --> 00:40:25,172
Leave.

484
00:40:26,132 --> 00:40:27,383
I'll take care of the rest.

485
00:40:35,141 --> 00:40:36,851
Why aren't you leaving?

486
00:40:39,687 --> 00:40:41,021
I'm sorry about yesterday.

487
00:40:43,899 --> 00:40:44,900
Actually,

488
00:40:46,444 --> 00:40:48,320
there's something I haven't told you.

489
00:40:49,029 --> 00:40:51,407
What is it that you haven't told me?

490
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:53,701
The truth is…

491
00:40:55,786 --> 00:40:57,872
At some point,
going on stage started to scare me.

492
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:01,917
I'm fine when I play by myself,

493
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:06,505
but thinking about the stage
makes me break out in a cold sweat,

494
00:41:06,589 --> 00:41:08,007
and I can't breathe.

495
00:41:08,966 --> 00:41:12,178
I think that's why I kept missing
or showing up late to practice.

496
00:41:13,637 --> 00:41:14,472
Why?

497
00:41:16,849 --> 00:41:17,850
Is it…

498
00:41:19,518 --> 00:41:20,895
because of what happened that day?

499
00:41:23,522 --> 00:41:24,648
Yeah.

500
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:31,030
I tried to get over it, but it's not easy.

501
00:41:33,073 --> 00:41:35,576
I should've been honest from the start.

502
00:41:35,659 --> 00:41:36,702
I'm sorry.

503
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:46,128
Oh, right.

504
00:41:47,588 --> 00:41:49,798
I'll make sure Mr. Do understands,

505
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:51,091
so don't worry.

506
00:42:07,066 --> 00:42:08,317
<i>The grand prize goes to</i>

507
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:10,486
Choi Jeong-yo!

508
00:42:14,073 --> 00:42:15,950
There's a medical emergency.

509
00:42:16,033 --> 00:42:17,451
Mom!

510
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:20,037
- Mom!
- Ma'am?

511
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:23,082
Mom! You're okay, right?

512
00:42:23,165 --> 00:42:23,999
Mom!

513
00:42:26,126 --> 00:42:27,211
Mom.

514
00:42:27,294 --> 00:42:30,339
Mom. Mom!

515
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:05,749
<i>Did you tell Mr. Do what we talked about?</i>

516
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:08,752
<i>No. Why?</i>

517
00:43:13,674 --> 00:43:15,467
<i>Then don't tell him yet.</i>

518
00:43:15,551 --> 00:43:17,553
<i>Come to the small auditorium</i>
<i>tomorrow by 9 p.m.</i>

519
00:43:35,529 --> 00:43:36,447
What's all this?

520
00:43:40,075 --> 00:43:42,536
I told you yesterday
that I can't get on stage--

521
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:43,912
Just come in and sit down.

522
00:44:19,281 --> 00:44:20,658
If you're going to perform,

523
00:44:20,741 --> 00:44:22,701
you have to get used to the stage.

524
00:44:23,786 --> 00:44:26,205
If you start out playing
like you're not onstage

525
00:44:26,288 --> 00:44:27,915
and gradually increase the pressure,

526
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:30,459
you'll be fine in no time.

527
00:44:36,632 --> 00:44:38,509
You're not the only one with stage fright.

528
00:44:40,511 --> 00:44:41,970
The degree may vary,

529
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:45,683
but all performers experience it.

530
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:48,519
You just have to face it and deal with it.

531
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:51,063
Avoiding it won't do any good.

532
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:55,567
So?

533
00:44:56,944 --> 00:44:57,986
Think you can do it?

534
00:45:03,701 --> 00:45:04,827
I'll give it a try.

535
00:48:02,045 --> 00:48:03,005
What time is it?

536
00:48:05,215 --> 00:48:06,091
It's 1 a.m.?

537
00:48:07,092 --> 00:48:08,051
It's 1 a.m.?

538
00:48:20,230 --> 00:48:21,148
Huh?

539
00:48:21,231 --> 00:48:23,358
Hey, why are all the lights turned off?

540
00:48:23,442 --> 00:48:24,276
The door!

541
00:48:25,110 --> 00:48:26,904
They lock the door at this hour?

542
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:35,787
Why would they lock this up
with someone inside?

543
00:48:35,871 --> 00:48:38,790
They probably didn't think
anyone would be in the small auditorium.

544
00:48:47,382 --> 00:48:48,717
Who are you calling?

545
00:48:48,800 --> 00:48:50,802
We should at least tell
our homeroom teacher.

546
00:48:50,886 --> 00:48:51,720
Hey.

547
00:48:51,803 --> 00:48:53,722
I got into trouble not too long ago.

548
00:48:53,805 --> 00:48:55,849
What do you think they'll do to me
if they find out?

549
00:48:55,933 --> 00:48:57,309
What should we do then?

550
00:49:03,273 --> 00:49:04,608
Where are you going?

551
00:49:05,567 --> 00:49:06,526
Damn it.

552
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:10,155
This is a good spot. Lots of leaves too.

553
00:49:11,531 --> 00:49:13,075
Don't tell me you want us to jump.

554
00:49:17,621 --> 00:49:18,789
Wait, Choi Jeong-yo.

555
00:49:21,833 --> 00:49:24,628
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo! Are you okay?

556
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:26,713
Get down here already.

557
00:49:27,422 --> 00:49:29,216
You crazy bastard.

558
00:49:29,299 --> 00:49:30,258
Come on down.

559
00:49:32,594 --> 00:49:33,595
Hurry up!

560
00:49:57,119 --> 00:49:57,995
Let's go.

561
00:50:05,460 --> 00:50:06,753
That was fun, right?

562
00:50:06,837 --> 00:50:07,796
Whatever.

563
00:50:08,922 --> 00:50:11,967
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

564
00:50:26,064 --> 00:50:28,567
I'm the king of the world!

565
00:50:40,037 --> 00:50:41,121
Hey, you punks!

566
00:50:41,913 --> 00:50:43,749
What do you think you're doing?

567
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:47,169
- Hey, let's run.
- Okay.

568
00:50:47,961 --> 00:50:49,212
Stop right there!

569
00:50:50,088 --> 00:50:52,549
What class are you in?

570
00:51:17,032 --> 00:51:18,658
<i>Can we practice tomorrow too?</i>

571
00:51:21,953 --> 00:51:24,790
What's up with him? Why is he so eager?

572
00:51:29,878 --> 00:51:30,754
<i>All right.</i>

573
00:51:36,718 --> 00:51:37,844
All right.

574
00:51:37,928 --> 00:51:40,180
All right.

575
00:51:54,402 --> 00:51:55,654
What's wrong with you?

576
00:51:55,737 --> 00:51:56,696
Just open the door.

577
00:51:59,116 --> 00:52:00,075
Get inside.

578
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:01,701
Hurry up.

579
00:52:24,975 --> 00:52:26,393
<i>Let's go somewhere tomorrow.</i>

580
00:52:29,729 --> 00:52:30,564
<i>Where?</i>

581
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:36,444
<i>You'll see when we get there.</i>

582
00:52:44,661 --> 00:52:46,705
Come on, fill me in.

583
00:52:46,788 --> 00:52:48,248
Where are we going?

584
00:52:48,999 --> 00:52:50,292
You'll see when we get there.

585
00:52:52,085 --> 00:52:53,295
Jeez.

586
00:53:11,104 --> 00:53:12,147
What is this?

587
00:53:13,315 --> 00:53:15,275
You want us to perform here?

588
00:53:15,358 --> 00:53:17,903
We need to see if you can play
in front of an audience.

589
00:53:19,070 --> 00:53:19,905
Hey.

590
00:53:20,655 --> 00:53:22,782
I'm not ready to do this yet.

591
00:53:23,491 --> 00:53:25,035
I'm really sorry.

592
00:53:27,370 --> 00:53:29,414
Nobody here knows who you are.

593
00:53:29,497 --> 00:53:31,583
They don't care one bit about you.

594
00:53:31,666 --> 00:53:33,418
It'll be easier here than on a real stage.

595
00:53:33,501 --> 00:53:35,170
That's just your opinion!

596
00:53:36,671 --> 00:53:39,341
If it were that easy,
do you think I would've struggled so much?

597
00:53:40,884 --> 00:53:42,219
I can't do it.

598
00:53:42,302 --> 00:53:44,387
How long are you going to
keep playing in hiding?

599
00:53:45,096 --> 00:53:46,890
It's time to come out of your cave!

600
00:53:51,186 --> 00:53:53,063
I know this is hard for you.

601
00:53:53,146 --> 00:53:55,607
But ignoring the problem
won't solve anything.

602
00:53:56,441 --> 00:53:58,818
You need to face it at some point.

603
00:54:00,737 --> 00:54:02,239
If you can't look at the people,

604
00:54:02,989 --> 00:54:04,658
pretend we're practicing and look at me.

605
00:54:05,951 --> 00:54:07,535
Pretend there's no audience.

606
00:54:08,370 --> 00:54:09,663
Just focus on my playing.

607
00:54:52,497 --> 00:54:54,582
<i>If you start out playing</i>
<i>like you're not on stage,</i>

608
00:54:55,292 --> 00:54:58,169
<i>then gradually increase the pressure,</i>
<i>you'll be fine in no time.</i>

609
00:55:01,298 --> 00:55:03,133
<i>You're not the only one with stage fright.</i>

610
00:55:03,216 --> 00:55:05,844
<i>All performers have it.</i>

611
00:55:06,594 --> 00:55:08,638
<i>You just have to face it and deal with it.</i>

612
00:55:09,180 --> 00:55:11,182
<i>Avoiding it won't do any good.</i>

613
00:57:28,194 --> 00:57:31,948
<i>The train approaching</i>
<i>is bound for Sinhadam.</i>

614
00:57:32,031 --> 00:57:34,492
<i>Please take a step back.</i>

615
00:58:38,681 --> 00:58:40,808
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

616
00:58:40,892 --> 00:58:42,810
<i>You don't follow the sheet music.</i>

617
00:58:42,894 --> 00:58:45,438
<i>I think Chopin would say it's fine.</i>

618
00:58:45,522 --> 00:58:47,106
Audition for the concerto.

619
00:58:47,190 --> 00:58:50,443
Didn't your grandfather tell you
he asked to see Choi Jeong-yo?

620
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:52,487
<i>I didn't play a duet with you</i>
<i>because I wanted to.</i>

621
00:58:52,570 --> 00:58:54,864
<i>One minute you're nice, then you're mad.</i>
<i>Make up your mind, damn it.</i>

622
00:58:54,948 --> 00:58:55,907
What the hell is it then?

623
00:58:55,990 --> 00:58:57,825
- What's going on?
- Stop them! Hey!

624
00:58:59,786 --> 00:59:00,703
Mom.

625
00:59:02,580 --> 00:59:04,082
<i>Don't think about anything.</i>

626
00:59:04,165 --> 00:59:05,208
<i>Just focus on my voice</i>

627
00:59:05,833 --> 00:59:07,710
<i>and my playing.</i>

628
00:59:09,170 --> 00:59:14,175
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
